  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "Tables 3 to 10 parsed from the PDF text layer (pdfplumber table extraction, specimen columns assigned from the header cells) and compared cell by cell with page images rendered at 2.6x; number resistant over number tested was also recomputed for every cell and all differences over 1 point are noted on the cell. Chart values (Figures 9, 11, 14, 16, 18, 20, 22) are printed data labels from the text layer: each label was assigned to the bar whose end it sits next to on the same row, the series from the legend swatch colours, and the bar length measured against the axis ticks agreed with the label within 0.1 point for every bar; 0% labels of zero-length bars were placed by row position; every chart was also checked by eye on the rendered page. Page numbers are PDF page numbers, which equal the printed page numbers in this report."
 },
 "notes": "First annual report of AARSNET, the Assam state AMR surveillance network under NCDC (nodal centre Gauhati Medical College and Hospital, 12 government medical colleges): 14,179 priority-pathogen isolates from 13,369 unique patients in 2025 (the Discussion gives different totals: 14,346 reported, 11,834 and 13,299 after deduplication). Values are % resistant as printed. Genus-level organisms as printed. Pus aspirate (aspirated purulent material from a closed infected site; pus and wound swabs excluded) is mapped to deep; other sterile body fluids (CSF, pleural, peritoneal, synovial, pericardial) to sterile; IPD to ward. Location rows pool all specimens and carry no n (not printed with the charts); Table 4 location counts are recorded as counts. Several location figures do not reconcile with the specimen tables (S. aureus linezolid, Pseudomonas gentamicin, E. coli co-trimoxazole), see cell notes. Table 4 location counts do not sum to the Table 3 totals for Klebsiella (2,861 against 2,890), Pseudomonas (1,121 against 1,065) and S. aureus (1,684 against 1,711).",
